DYNAMIC CONTEXT LOADING (NEW)

To prevent context overload the system must dynamically load documentation.

Step 1 — Identify task scope

Determine feature/module involved.

Step 2 — Load minimal architecture context

Load only:

code-map
feature-boundaries

Step 3 — Load relevant feature docs

Load only documentation related to the feature being modified.

Examples:

Auth feature → load auth-flow.md
API feature → load api-routes.md
Database feature → load database.md

Step 4 — Load file indexes

Load only indexes relevant to target files.

Step 5 — Load debugging docs if task is bug fix.

This system ensures minimal context usage while maintaining reasoning accuracy.

